; The C flags of every library, test and bench under packages/rig. A C warning is
; an error in every profile but release, which must not break on a warning a
; future compiler adds.
;
; The sanitize profile, run on Linux, compiles the C with AddressSanitizer and
; UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer and links the sanitizer runtimes into every
; executable, whose link_flags keep :standard to carry them. Its options: a
; report ends the process, leaks are not errors, a domain's thread exits on
; the signal stack the OCaml runtime allocated, which AddressSanitizer would
; unmap as its own, an allocation the allocator refuses returns NULL as libc's
; does, so the library's answer to a refusal is what a test sees, and the
; shadow gap is left unprotected, since CUDA and NV map GPU addresses below
; 2^40 in it.
;
; The sanitize profile also stresses the collector and links the debug
; runtime, so a value a stub holds unrooted, or memory a finaliser frees while
; it is still used, fails at once. OCAMLRUNPARAM gives a 32 KiB minor heap
; (s=4k), major cycles far more often (o=20), pushed at once by custom blocks
; (M=1, m=1), and a heap check at the end of each (V=1); v=0 silences the
; debug runtime's banner, which a cram test would read as output.
;
; Benches run with `dune build @bench`, never in runtest, each under the lock
; %{workspace_root}/bench. A suite or bench that acts on a GPU also takes
; %{workspace_root}/gpu, so one build runs one at a time. A bench's C that calls a library's C sits in a
; library: GNU ld resolves it only from an archive listed after the caller.
;
; WINDTRAP_TIMEOUT bounds each test that sets no ~timeout, so a hung test
; cannot block the shared watch server.

(env
 (release
  (odoc (warnings fatal))
  (c_flags
   (:standard -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra))
  (env-vars
   (WINDTRAP_TIMEOUT 60)))
 (sanitize
  (odoc (warnings fatal))
  (c_flags
   (:standard
    -std=c11
    -Wall
    -Wextra
    -Werror
    -g
    -fno-omit-frame-pointer
    -fsanitize=address,undefined))
  (link_flags
   (:standard -runtime-variant d -cclib -fsanitize=address,undefined))
  (env-vars
   (OCAMLRUNPARAM s=4k,o=20,M=1,m=1,V=1,v=0)
   (ASAN_OPTIONS
    halt_on_error=1:detect_leaks=0:use_sigaltstack=0:allocator_may_return_null=1:protect_shadow_gap=0)
   (UBSAN_OPTIONS halt_on_error=1:print_stacktrace=1)
   (WINDTRAP_TIMEOUT 60)))
 (_
  (odoc (warnings fatal))
  (c_flags
   (:standard -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror))
  (env-vars
   (WINDTRAP_TIMEOUT 60))))

; README.md's program runs under mdx. dune links mdx's toplevel without the
; profile's link_flags, so rig's sanitized stubs cannot link into it.

(mdx
 (files README.md)
 (package rig)
 (enabled_if
  (<> %{profile} sanitize))
 (libraries rig))
